// ===================== NPC COMBAT DEFS =====================
// Combat-ready stat blocks for 29 of the 30 NPC_LIBRARY entries ("The Patron" is deliberately
// excluded -- per their own entry, nobody has ever met them in person, so there's no body to
// put on a battle map). Same shape as HUMAN_NPC_DEFS (see the main file) -- name/alignment/cr/
// ac/hitDice/ability scores/skills/saves, plus `actions` where a `{weapon, dice, dmgType,
// ability}` entry gets its to-hit and damage computed from the listed ability score and CR by
// the same humanNpcAttack() formula every other homebrew NPC in this app already uses (never
// hand-typed independently of the stat block, so numbers can't quietly drift out of sync), and
// a plain `{name, text}` entry is used as-is for anything that isn't a simple weapon swing
// (Rally the Line, Word of the Throne, Counterspell, and the like).
//
// HP/CON were derived directly from the flavor hp string already shown on each NPC's card (see
// NPC_LIBRARY above) -- same hit dice, same total, just decomposed into hitDice+con here so the
// combat version and the card version always read the same "165 (22d8 + 66)" at a glance. AC is
// carried over unchanged (humanNpc() takes it as a flat value, not auto-derived from DEX+armor,
// same as HUMAN_NPC_DEFS already does). CR is a rough narrative-power placement, not a strict
// DMG-by-defenses calculation -- consistent with how HUMAN_NPC_DEFS itself already treats CR
// (a "Human Guard" at CR 1/8 already runs hotter on AC than the DMG's own CR 1/8 benchmark).
//
// The main file maps this through humanNpc() (see CUSTOM_HUMAN_NPCS) into NPC_LIBRARY_MONSTERS
// and merges it into monsterDatabase, so every name here is selectable from the Combat tab's
// normal monster picker like any other creature.
